00:00:00,001 --> 00:00:06,000
You thought you had the basics pretty much figured out.

2
00:00:06,001 --> 00:00:08,000
Think again.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Science and technology are changing the way the world engages in its favorite pastime.

4
00:00:15,001 --> 00:00:19,000
Now, high-tech sex on Modern Marvels.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,560
High-tech sex?

6
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:38,860
It sounds like a contradiction in terms.

7
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:42,180
Isn't sex one thing that doesn't require any technology?

8
00:00:43,420 --> 00:00:45,080
It's a biological function,

9
00:00:45,700 --> 00:00:48,860
a drive for which people are pretty much fully equipped at birth.

10
00:00:51,380 --> 00:00:55,740
And yet, the human impulse to take a good thing and make it incredible

11
00:00:55,741 --> 00:01:04,580
has driven people since ancient times to contrive and devise potions, gadgets, devices, and toys for l'amour.

12
00:01:07,580 --> 00:01:16,860
Every technological advance from ceramics to silent films to CD-ROMs and DVDs has immediately been coupled with sex.

13
00:01:17,220 --> 00:01:24,360
It never ceases to amaze me the speed with which humans deploy their technology for sexual purposes.

14
00:01:25,140 --> 00:01:26,480
It's got to be some unit of measurement.

15
00:01:26,700 --> 00:01:28,600
It's like speed of light, speed of sound,

16
00:01:29,120 --> 00:01:31,680
time it takes to get technology to a sexual expression.

17
00:01:31,960 --> 00:01:33,600
Sex has never been totally natural.

18
00:01:33,780 --> 00:01:38,440
People have always been trying to insert some kind of mechanical device in it.

19
00:01:38,520 --> 00:01:40,140
They've been trying to toy with it.

20
00:01:40,260 --> 00:01:42,560
They've been trying to make it better.

21
00:01:42,561 --> 00:01:48,240
I mean, with this huge brain, we have created a high-tech world

22
00:01:48,241 --> 00:01:51,300
out of a very primitive, basic drive.

23
00:01:51,301 --> 00:01:56,020
That drive is on the verge of morphing into some mind-boggling new forms.

24
00:01:57,060 --> 00:02:02,940
Like holographic sex, in which a programmable 3D image floats to life before your eyes.

25
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:07,040
Or virtual sex, not just emails and chat rooms,

26
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:13,200
but sophisticated computer add-ons that make it possible to literally turn someone on across the Internet.

27
00:02:13,860 --> 00:02:19,440
As scientists isolate the chemistry of sex, the specific proteins that control desire and function,

28
00:02:19,441 --> 00:02:22,580
We really do stand on the edge of a new reality.

29
00:02:22,920 --> 00:02:31,760
Within a couple decades, when you look onto the Internet or look into the personals of a newspaper,

30
00:02:32,220 --> 00:02:35,460
a person might say, my name is Betty.

31
00:02:36,020 --> 00:02:43,440
I have high levels of MAO, low levels of serotonin, high testosterone, high dopamine.

32
00:02:44,160 --> 00:02:47,900
And if you are a biological match, call me.

33
00:02:49,440 --> 00:02:54,000
The call for psychosexual drugs stretches far into the past.

34
00:02:56,120 --> 00:03:01,900
Aphrodisiacs have captured the imagination and the investigative energies of nearly every culture since ancient times.

35
00:03:02,520 --> 00:03:05,760
The range of reputed aphrodisiacs is fascinating.

36
00:03:06,660 --> 00:03:13,560
Everything from onions to ginger, mandrake root to rhinoceros horn, swan genitals to Spanish fly.

37
00:03:13,561 --> 00:03:20,640
Most aphrodisiacs draw their mystique from one of four somewhat demystifying reasons.

38
00:03:21,540 --> 00:03:30,900
They look like sex organs, they're spicy and hot, they're extremely rare, or they are the sex organs of animals, especially animals known for their sexual energy.

39
00:03:31,660 --> 00:03:37,040
Which is not to say that aphrodisiacs don't sometimes have at least a partial basis in scientific truth.

40
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:38,560
Like oysters.

41
00:03:38,561 --> 00:03:47,000
They are so rich in iodine and zinc from the sea that they restore the body and bring vitality.

42
00:03:47,640 --> 00:03:51,200
And also they're very similar to certain body parts.

43
00:03:52,920 --> 00:03:56,480
Spanish fly, of course, is the bad boy of aphrodisiacs.

44
00:03:58,140 --> 00:04:01,840
Made from the crushed skin of a blister beetle prevalent in southern Europe,

45
00:04:02,220 --> 00:04:06,620
Spanish fly has been used as a sexual stimulant for at least 2,000 years.

46
00:04:06,621 --> 00:04:15,160
According to the Food and Drug Administration, Spanish fly has no special powers of arousal, but is dangerous and potentially lethal.

47
00:04:15,640 --> 00:04:24,820
It irritates the urinary system, so that any kind of rubbing or itching definitely satisfies or tries to satisfy the itch.

48
00:04:25,120 --> 00:04:28,060
But the problem is it causes urinary damage.

49
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:35,400
Ginseng, one of the most revered and mysterious plants on Earth, has long been hailed as a sexual tonic.

50
00:04:36,620 --> 00:04:42,840
In tests relating to sexuality, ginseng has been shown to increase sperm production and mobility.

51
00:04:43,620 --> 00:04:46,460
It has also quickened the development of sexual organs in mice.

52
00:04:47,880 --> 00:04:51,600
The plant is highly valued by those who believe in its tonic powers.

53
00:04:52,220 --> 00:04:55,620
Most ginseng sells for between $100 and $500 a pound.

54
00:04:57,940 --> 00:05:01,180
This 40-year-old root is priced at $16,000.

55
00:05:02,200 --> 00:05:03,240
But that's nothing.

56
00:05:03,241 --> 00:05:10,800
In 2001, the owner of this herb store in Los Angeles sold a single ginseng root for $180,000.

57
00:05:12,720 --> 00:05:16,300
Most of the most expensive roots come originally from the Qingbai Mountains in China.

58
00:05:17,740 --> 00:05:24,040
And the root that are in hundreds of thousands of dollars, number one, is based on how it looks, like a man.

59
00:05:24,340 --> 00:05:27,760
It's really thin, it's got the full growth root, it's got the long legs.

60
00:05:28,780 --> 00:05:31,200
Also another thing is, how old is it?

61
00:05:31,201 --> 00:05:36,160
The older a root, the more active ingredients or ginsenosides it has

62
00:05:36,161 --> 00:05:40,520
Ginseng isn't the only prized aphrodisiac in Chinese medicine

63
00:05:40,521 --> 00:05:42,060
Far from it

64
00:05:42,061 --> 00:05:44,820
What we have here is deer antler

65
00:05:44,821 --> 00:05:47,680
People say these are aphrodisiacs

66
00:05:47,681 --> 00:05:51,840
Just because they increase the red blood cells in the system and testosterone levels

67
00:05:51,841 --> 00:05:57,060
Other Chinese herbs that we use to tonify the yang for sexual performance is a gecko

68
00:05:57,061 --> 00:06:00,300
Which is basically a lizard from China

69
00:06:00,301 --> 00:06:02,740
very good for the kidneys.

70
00:06:03,980 --> 00:06:07,280
We also have an assortment of seahorses,

71
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:09,560
good for impotence,

72
00:06:10,020 --> 00:06:12,660
and good for tonifying the yang.

73
00:06:15,560 --> 00:06:18,900
Western medicine may not know much about tonifying the yang,

74
00:06:19,040 --> 00:06:22,320
but it has come up with a stunningly effective potency pill of its own.

75
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:25,980
Viagra, introduced in March 1998,

76
00:06:26,520 --> 00:06:29,840
currently generates over a billion and a half dollars a year in sales.

77
00:06:30,300 --> 00:06:37,900
An estimated 52% of all men between 40 and 70 years old have experienced some kind of erectile dysfunction,

78
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:41,860
a condition which for millennia has been suffered in helpless silence.

79
00:06:43,380 --> 00:06:47,720
Before Viagra, an erection injection was the main remedy for ED.

80
00:06:49,080 --> 00:06:57,380
These are injections directly into the penis of substances which make the vessels of the penis grow larger and the penis erect.

81
00:06:57,381 --> 00:07:03,000
And not surprisingly, men were not desperately keen to inject needles into their penis.

82
00:07:04,920 --> 00:07:13,020
Sildenafil, the active ingredient in Viagra, was developed by Pfizer Pharmaceuticals in 1989 as a heart drug for people with angina.

83
00:07:14,480 --> 00:07:19,460
It didn't perform well in tests, but male volunteers did report a curious side effect.

84
00:07:20,480 --> 00:07:22,580
They were getting erections very easily.

85
00:07:23,160 --> 00:07:26,780
For example, just a pretty nurse passing was sufficient to give them an erection.

86
00:07:27,380 --> 00:07:31,240
Pfizer quickly shifted the focus of its tests.

87
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:37,820
Using a device called Origiscan, it measured the erections of thousands of men under the influence of the new drug.

88
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:41,480
80% reported improved erections.

89
00:07:42,120 --> 00:07:43,060
Pfizer was ecstatic.

90
00:07:43,620 --> 00:07:44,640
So were the volunteers.

91
00:07:45,400 --> 00:07:49,680
We are required by the regulations to account for every last tablet.

92
00:07:50,380 --> 00:07:54,540
Towards the end of the study, we found that patients were reluctant to give their tablets back.

93
00:07:55,120 --> 00:08:00,580
So they tended to be more active towards the end of a study than they were at the start of the study.

94
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:07,060
And this is probably because they knew that the tablets were running out and they'd have to give them back.

95
00:08:08,840 --> 00:08:11,500
Sildenafil works by increasing blood flow to the penis.

96
00:08:12,540 --> 00:08:15,660
It does this by boosting the impact of nitric oxide,

97
00:08:15,661 --> 00:08:19,960
a substance which is released by nerves in the penis following sexual stimulation

98
00:08:19,961 --> 00:08:24,520
and which causes its vessels to dilate, making an erection possible.

99
00:08:24,540 --> 00:08:34,280
One of the volunteers in the Viagra tests happened to be Senator and 1996 presidential candidate Bob Dole.

100
00:08:35,240 --> 00:08:37,160
You know, it's a little embarrassing to talk about ED,

101
00:08:38,100 --> 00:08:42,920
but it's so important to millions of men and their partners that I decide to talk about it publicly.

102
00:08:43,340 --> 00:08:48,780
People identified with him straight away, and if it was okay for Bob Dole to talk about erectile dysfunction,

103
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:52,400
then it was okay for anybody else to talk about erectile dysfunction.

104
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:55,080
Thinking about trying Viagra?

105
00:08:55,420 --> 00:08:58,440
We wanted somebody also to open the door for the younger man.

106
00:09:01,480 --> 00:09:03,020
So get in the driver's seat.

107
00:09:03,900 --> 00:09:08,140
Get to your doctor for a checkup and find out if a free sample of Viagra is right for you.

108
00:09:08,141 --> 00:09:16,560
And what Mark Martin does is he puts sexual dysfunction in the context of overall health with the Tune Up for Life campaign.

109
00:09:16,561 --> 00:09:24,620
Despite its phenomenal success, Pfizer estimates that only 20% of those who could benefit from Viagra are taking the drug.

110
00:09:26,020 --> 00:09:30,160
Which is one reason why pharmaceutical firms are feverishly working on alternatives.

111
00:09:30,900 --> 00:09:34,740
Like this gel form of sildenafil, which works directly on the penis.

112
00:09:35,980 --> 00:09:45,440
And this fast-acting inhalant, which sends irreversible messages of arousal to the brain and triggers an erection within 15 minutes.

113
00:09:47,540 --> 00:09:50,140
Incredibly, new treatments for ED are in the offing

114
00:09:50,141 --> 00:09:53,500
that will eventually make Viagra and its spin-off seem passe.

115
00:09:54,660 --> 00:09:57,880
Gene therapy will probably be available within 10 years.

116
00:09:58,560 --> 00:10:01,620
When doctors isolate the specific genes that control erection,

117
00:10:02,260 --> 00:10:05,260
they'll be able to introduce those genes through a benign virus

118
00:10:05,261 --> 00:10:09,220
and rebuild a man's erectile system from the inside out.

119
00:10:09,480 --> 00:10:16,160
Gene therapy means the application of segments of genes

120
00:10:16,161 --> 00:10:25,380
which are segments of chromosomes, into a diseased organ to replace the abnormal genes

121
00:10:25,381 --> 00:10:30,340
and correct the abnormality and return that organ to normal function.

122
00:10:32,360 --> 00:10:37,380
An even more staggering high-tech treatment for ED is tissue engineering.

123
00:10:39,440 --> 00:10:44,100
Men or women with genitals that don't work and don't respond to any other treatment

124
00:10:44,101 --> 00:10:47,740
will literally be able to grow a new penis or vagina.

125
00:10:48,380 --> 00:10:50,160
It's no longer science fiction.

126
00:10:50,820 --> 00:10:53,320
We are able to take small pieces of tissue,

127
00:10:53,500 --> 00:10:55,640
grow them out in the laboratory, and create organs.

128
00:10:56,180 --> 00:10:58,540
Dr. Anthony Atala of Harvard Medical School

129
00:10:58,541 --> 00:11:00,620
has helped pioneer the process.

130
00:11:01,500 --> 00:11:04,040
Over the last 10 years, he has successfully grown

131
00:11:04,041 --> 00:11:06,540
new penises and vaginas for small animals,

132
00:11:07,080 --> 00:11:09,240
as well as bladders, windpipes, and other organs.

133
00:11:10,120 --> 00:11:13,240
Though it sounds a little like something out of Frankenstein,

134
00:11:13,241 --> 00:11:18,640
The process of tissue engineering is disarmingly straightforward and low-key.

135
00:11:20,060 --> 00:11:23,960
Atala and his team biopsy a small piece of healthy tissue from the damaged organ,

136
00:11:24,400 --> 00:11:27,540
then grow the tissue in this red culture, or soup.

137
00:11:28,640 --> 00:11:34,060
When the cells have multiplied, they are basted onto and injected into a scaffold, or mold,

138
00:11:34,580 --> 00:11:39,840
which is made out of biodegradable materials and carefully shaped into the form of the desired organ,

139
00:11:40,120 --> 00:11:42,500
in this case, a small vagina.

140
00:11:43,240 --> 00:11:47,740
The seeding process, as it is called, goes on for seven days.

141
00:11:49,520 --> 00:11:53,920
These scaffolds degrade as the tissue is forming.

142
00:11:54,880 --> 00:12:00,060
And by the time that the scaffold is fully degraded, the tissue is now fully formed.

143
00:12:00,780 --> 00:12:03,520
This radical treatment won't replace Viagra.

144
00:12:04,080 --> 00:12:07,220
But it will be a godsend for those born with non-functioning organs,

145
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:09,640
or organs that have been damaged through violence.

146
00:12:10,280 --> 00:12:12,780
Or even for men with severe cases of ED.

147
00:12:13,240 --> 00:12:15,540
where the penile tissue is thoroughly scarred.

148
00:12:17,720 --> 00:12:19,840
Someday, patients who have sexual dysfunction

149
00:12:19,841 --> 00:12:22,200
will be able to go to their doctors and say,

150
00:12:22,340 --> 00:12:24,360
you know, we've tried everything,

151
00:12:24,460 --> 00:12:26,120
and the problem is on the organ itself,

152
00:12:26,540 --> 00:12:30,400
and hopefully we will be able to put a new tissue or organ

153
00:12:30,401 --> 00:12:31,580
back into that patient

154
00:12:31,581 --> 00:12:35,200
so that they are able to have fulfilling lives.

155
00:12:36,580 --> 00:12:39,800
Dr. Atala expects tissue engineering for sexual organs

156
00:12:39,801 --> 00:12:42,100
to be available by 2010.

157
00:12:43,240 --> 00:12:45,340
Reviving men sexually is one thing.

158
00:12:45,800 --> 00:12:47,980
Helping them enjoy sex responsibly is another.

159
00:12:48,700 --> 00:12:52,160
Up next, the condom revolution and the male pill.

160
00:12:53,720 --> 00:12:57,120
In 1998, the year that Viagra was first available,

161
00:12:57,660 --> 00:13:01,380
the Pentagon spent $50 million on the drug for troops and veterans.

162
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:04,280
High-tech sex will return on Modern Marvels.

163
00:13:05,980 --> 00:13:08,420
While women have over a dozen options,

164
00:13:08,421 --> 00:13:12,180
when it comes to contraception for men, the condom is still king.

165
00:13:13,240 --> 00:13:18,180
The condom. Could anything be more homely and low-tech?

166
00:13:19,440 --> 00:13:23,560
And yet for all its simplicity, the condom has morphed into countless variations

167
00:13:23,561 --> 00:13:26,560
and evolved dramatically in recent years.

168
00:13:27,520 --> 00:13:33,040
We've seen new shapes, new materials, emphasis on pleasure, not just protection.

169
00:13:33,420 --> 00:13:37,160
We've seen polyurethanes, latex thinner than we could ever imagine.

170
00:13:37,360 --> 00:13:41,040
We've eliminated nasty smells and added strawberry aromas.

171
00:13:41,041 --> 00:13:43,920
We've come a long way in the condom industry.

172
00:13:44,660 --> 00:13:48,460
The technology behind condom production has also come a long way.

173
00:13:50,520 --> 00:13:53,900
700 million condoms are produced in the U.S. each year,

174
00:13:54,700 --> 00:13:57,160
mostly by dipping glass molds into latex.

175
00:13:58,420 --> 00:14:02,520
The dry condoms are rolled off the molds, washed, dried again,

176
00:14:02,860 --> 00:14:07,100
and then put through a series of stress tests to make sure they meet FDA standards.

177
00:14:07,840 --> 00:14:09,260
The stakes here are not small.

178
00:14:09,261 --> 00:14:17,320
This is a $1 device that's made for pennies that we are depending on to save our lives and prevent unwanted pregnancies.

179
00:14:18,620 --> 00:14:24,140
The AIDS crisis of the 1980s brought a sense of both urgency and creativity to condoms,

180
00:14:24,420 --> 00:14:28,100
which today come in many sizes and flavors.

181
00:14:29,660 --> 00:14:33,100
Some condoms are as thin as cellophane and virtually invisible.

182
00:14:33,101 --> 00:14:40,140
Some are lubricated with a desensitizing agent to help men who suffer from premature ejaculation.

183
00:14:41,140 --> 00:14:45,840
But the big commercial breakthrough in state-of-the-art condoms has to do with pleasure.

184
00:14:46,100 --> 00:14:47,740
These are our pleasure-producing condoms.

185
00:14:47,860 --> 00:14:49,960
This is the Pleasure Plus and this is the Inspiral.

186
00:14:50,320 --> 00:14:57,560
And you can see these crazy pouches and spirals are located exactly where most of the nerve endings are located.

187
00:14:58,880 --> 00:15:02,280
Anatomically designed to improve rather than get in the way of sex,

188
00:15:03,140 --> 00:15:07,020
Pleasure condoms quickly became the fastest-growing segment of the condom business

189
00:15:07,021 --> 00:15:09,640
and changed the way men thought about protection.

190
00:15:10,340 --> 00:15:13,840
So the first time, it wasn't just buckle your seatbelt.

191
00:15:14,420 --> 00:15:17,800
It was now buckle your seatbelt and we're going to take you on a great ride.

192
00:15:17,801 --> 00:15:20,260
It was buckle that seatbelt because you're getting on a roller coaster.

193
00:15:20,660 --> 00:15:22,020
And that was a new idea.

194
00:15:23,300 --> 00:15:25,600
This may be the golden age of condoms,

195
00:15:26,200 --> 00:15:29,600
but the idea of sheathing the penis has been around for a very long time.

196
00:15:30,600 --> 00:15:34,760
The Egyptians made the first such sheaths, from papyrus, soaked in water.

197
00:15:35,740 --> 00:15:38,180
The ancient Chinese used oiled silk paper.

198
00:15:40,040 --> 00:15:44,760
Europeans in the 17th century made condoms out of fish bladders and animal gut.

199
00:15:44,980 --> 00:15:49,760
There were some pretty chunky condoms that had seams,

200
00:15:50,120 --> 00:15:54,900
and these were seams that protruded and that hurt men and women during high-friction sex.

201
00:15:54,901 --> 00:16:06,344
And then there were finer, more expensive models called gold beater skins in which intestinal matter was worked through chemicals and through just kind of hand beating

202
00:16:06,345 --> 00:16:08,400
into a very fine, supple mass.

203
00:16:10,120 --> 00:16:20,380
The vulcanization of rubber in 1844 had a revolutionary impact on condoms, turning them into rubbers that could be mass produced for pennies.

204
00:16:20,381 --> 00:16:26,600
No less a figure than George Bernard Shaw hailed the rubber condom and the sexual liberation it promised

205
00:16:26,601 --> 00:16:30,280
As the single best thing to come out of the Industrial Revolution

206
00:16:30,281 --> 00:16:35,880
Despite their widespread use, the U.S. government regarded condoms moralistically

207
00:16:35,881 --> 00:16:41,600
The Comstock Law of 1873 made all forms of birth control illegal

208
00:16:41,760 --> 00:16:47,320
And American soldiers were the only soldiers who didn't find condoms in their field kits during World War I

209
00:16:48,320 --> 00:16:53,600
Not surprisingly, Americans came home with more cases of syphilis and gonorrhea than other troops.

210
00:16:54,120 --> 00:16:58,920
When a man came back from a leave, he was asked whether he had sex.

211
00:16:58,921 --> 00:17:08,800
If he admitted to having sex, he was forced to go through a very nasty medical exam where his penis was smeared with a chemical ointment

212
00:17:08,801 --> 00:17:12,700
and his urethra was injected with a chemical substance,

213
00:17:12,860 --> 00:17:18,500
both of which were designed to protect them from contracting this disease

214
00:17:18,501 --> 00:17:20,700
even after the fact of having sex.

215
00:17:20,860 --> 00:17:23,700
This was painful, it was degrading, it didn't work.

216
00:17:24,580 --> 00:17:27,580
The military did an about-face in World War II,

217
00:17:28,240 --> 00:17:32,260
not only distributing condoms, but aggressively encouraging soldiers to use them.

218
00:17:32,680 --> 00:17:37,180
Well, there's only one sure preventative, and that's to keep your 13 buttons buttoned.

219
00:17:37,181 --> 00:17:39,000
The next best preventative is a rubber.

220
00:17:39,260 --> 00:17:41,800
Hell, a rubber's like taking a shower with a raincoat on.

221
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:45,380
A rubber is the most effective single pro there is, if put on soon enough.

222
00:17:47,960 --> 00:17:51,700
Condoms were finally established as an acceptable method of disease prevention.

223
00:17:52,400 --> 00:17:56,940
The only problem was decades of underground production had made them incredibly unreliable.

224
00:17:58,040 --> 00:18:02,780
Nearly 60% of all condoms proved defective in tests conducted before the war.

